<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diet of Schwäbisch Hall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1190">1190</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Diet of Schwäbisch Hall was an imperial assembly held in 1190 at Schwäbisch Hall in Swabia under King Henry VI. It ruled that the ducal authority of Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Louvain</a> applied only to his own lands, reducing the old duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-lower-lorraine">Lower Lotharingia</a> to a title. His territories around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and Leuven thus became the Duchy of Brabant.</p></div>
